					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3623925#post-3594774</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-3623925/scp-80s-j#post-3594774</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 16 Sep 2017 09:08:06 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>dankaar</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1790336</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Yes and no.</p> <p>What everyone remembers as the &quot;It&quot; movie (with Tim Curry as Pennywise) was actually a TV miniseries. And that one did take place in the 50's. At least, for the scenes involving the cast as children.</p> <p>The new one that came out (with Bill Skarsgård as Pennywise) moved the children's encounter timeframe up to the 1980's; that way there, when part II comes out, they can film it as happening in 2016 instead of the 1980s (as with the Tim Curry version).</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
